{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And as for you, lift up your staff and stretch out your hand over the sea.</b> In the Midrash (Exodus Rabbah 21:9) they said: because the Egyptians were saying, 'Were it not for the staff, he would not have been able to perform all the miracles,' therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said, 'Remove your staff and stretch out your hand' — for 'lift up' (הָרֵם) means removal. And I shall give a reason for the matter, why specifically at the splitting of the Sea of Reeds the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded to remove the staff: it is because the Holy One, blessed be He, wanted Moses to make below a model corresponding to everything done above. Now all the plagues were performed by 'the finger of Elohim' (Exodus 8:19), and therefore they were also performed below by means of the staff of Moses, for the staff resembles a finger. But against the sea they were stricken with the entire hand, as it says, 'And Israel saw the great hand' etc. (Exodus 14:31). Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Moses that he should also make below a model corresponding to this, and remove the staff which resembles a finger, and 'stretch out your hand' — the entire hand, a model of the mighty hand above, blessed be He. Therefore it says, 'And Israel saw the great hand,' and along with this they saw that it was not by the power of the staff that Moses performed this great and awesome deed, for he needed to stretch out his hand as a model of the mighty hand above. Therefore, 'and they believed in HaShem and in Moses His servant' (Exodus 14:31), for they retracted what they had said previously — that by the power of the staff he had wrought all this." "And from here you will truly understand what the sin of Moses was at the waters of Meribah, for there it is stated in precisely the opposite manner from what is stated here. For here it says, 'Lift up your staff' (הָרֵם אֶת מַטְּךָ) — that is, remove your staff — 'and stretch out your hand' (וּנְטֵה אֶת יָדְךָ), and through this they came to faith. But there it says, 'And he raised his hand and struck with his staff' (Numbers 20:11) — he removed his hand, for he did not perform the action with his hand but with his staff, and therefore he restored the earlier statements — that by the power of the staff he had wrought everything — to their place, and in this he caused a diminution of faith, as it is written, 'Because you did not believe in Me' (Numbers 20:12). And this matter will be explained, with the help of HaShem, thoroughly in its place in the portion of Ḥukkat (20:8)."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:20:08.400145410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}